'''Basic helix-loop-helix family, member a9''' is a [[protein]] in humans that is encoded by the BHLHA9 [[gene]].<ref name="entrez">{{cite web | title = Entrez Gene: Basic helix-loop-helix family, member a9 | url = https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene?db=gene&cmd=retrieve&list_uids=727857 | access-date = 2012-04-26 <!-- T14:09:35.140173-08:00 --> }}</ref> This protein is a [[transcription factor]] that is involved in the development of limbs through regulating genes related to limb [[morphogenesis]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q7RTU4/entry|title=Class A basic helix-loop-helix protein 9|publisher=UniProt consortium|access-date=2026-10-25}}</ref>

